Apprise Music bundles source vendored from third-party open-source projects.

## Audio analysis and smart playback tracking

The C++ audio analysis modules (mel spectrogram, STFT, resampler, tempo analysis)
in app/src/main/cpp/analyzer/ and the Kotlin trackers (BeatTracker, VocalTracker)
in app/src/main/kotlin/.../playback/smart/ are adapted from Orchard
(https://github.com/SFG5453/Orchard), Copyright (C) 2026 SFG545, licensed under
the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later (AGPL-3.0-or-later). Per AGPLv3
Section 13, these components are combined with Apprise Music (licensed under GPL-3.0).

## Lyrics providers

The provider clients and lyric parsers in lyrics/.../lyrics/bitchord are
adapted from BitChord (https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord),
Copyright its contributors, licensed under GPL-3.0. See LICENSE.

## Flamingo lyrics and player controls

The renderer in app/.../ui/component/flamingo and player chrome values
are adapted from Flamingo (https://github.com/shouryadixitisverycool/Flamingo),
by Yos-X and contributors, licensed under GPL-3.0. See LICENSE.

## hig module

Portions of the `hig/` module are vendored from compose-hig
(https://github.com/ienground/compose-hig), Copyright (c) IENGROUND of IENLAB
and prior contributors (Compose Cupertino project, Scott Lanoue), licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See hig/LICENSE for details.

## Artwork transitions

The artwork transition timing in `artwork/` is adapted from MeloX-Android
(https://github.com/lladlam/MeloX-Android), licensed under GPL-3.0.
See the repository LICENSE for details.

## Pre-trained machine learning models

- Beat This! beat tracking model (assets/beat_this_u8.onnx): Adapted from CPJKU/beat_this
  (https://github.com/CPJKU/beat_this), Johannes Kepler University Linz, licensed under MIT.
- MDX-Net vocal separation model (assets/uvr_mdxnet_9482.onnx): Ultimate Vocal Remover
  MDX-Net architecture by UVR Community / Kuielab.

## Base project

Apprise Music was originally built on an open-source GPL-3.0 music player base and has diverged
into an offline-first player. It remains licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE).
